      {
        "id": "af2bf6c9-9890-4461-8a19-8a892cf1c226",
        "locale": "en",
        "status": "draft",
        "document": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Rubali Valerio Calcaño, known as El Rubí del Acordeón, is a Dominican merengue típico singer and accordionist. Born in Santo Domingo on May 9, 1998, she grew up in Santiago de los Caballeros.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Musical training",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Her father, accordionist Lupe Valerio, taught her the instrument. She developed her singing at the «Ñico Lora» traditional music school in Santiago and performed with «Los Hijos de Lupe».",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Career",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "She moved to the United States in 2016 and resumed her musical practice in 2021. By 2023 she was introducing her own ensemble under her father's musical direction. Her recorded repertoire includes «Amor Prohibido» and «El Vecinito».",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Legacy",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Her work carries a family tradition of accordion playing into her own career as a singer and instrumental performer of merengue típico.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "revision": 1,
        "created_at": "2026-10-16T13:29:55.827385+00:00",
        "updated_at": "2026-10-16T13:29:55.827385+00:00",
        "document_type": "artist_biography",
